;; FOUND by the ESH-0101 guard coverage gate. Ledger: SW-87.
;; NATIVE ONLY (jit, aot-o0, aot-o2). Both VM axes run this correctly.
;;
;; codegenGuard binds the guard variable to an SSA VALUE
;; (symbol_table[var_name] = raised_tagged) rather than to an entry-block
;; alloca, so it is not a real binding. Two consequences, one loud per form and
;; one loud per MODULE:
;;
;;   (a) `set!` on it is rejected:
;;         ERROR: set!: variable 'e' is not mutable
;;                (not an alloca, global, or capture pointer)
;;
;;   (b) CAPTURING it in a closure fails LLVM module verification outright,
;;       because the value is defined in the handler block and the capture does
;;       not dominate its uses:
;;         Failed to generate LLVM IR from batch
;;         ERROR: LLVM module verification failed:
;;                Instruction does not dominate all uses!
;;       (b) takes the whole compilation unit down, not just the offending form.
;;
;; R7RS derives `guard` through `(let ((var condition)) ...)`, and a let-bound
;; variable is both assignable and capturable.
;;
;; want: (mutated orig) captured-value
(display (guard (e (#t (set! e (list 'mutated e)) e)) (raise 'orig)))
(display " ")
(define captured (guard (e (#t (lambda () e))) (raise 'captured-value)))
(display (captured))
(newline)
